When I first compiled the 3.4.x tree myself - many moons ago now - I had 
the very same problem. Blue was almost impossible to see, and some of the 
other darker colours weren't much better...

The fix that I found was a registry file someone had made and posted on the 
internet that alters the RGB values of the console colour values. 
Unfortunatly I've no idea where I found it, but I do know that it's out 
there somewhere... :)

In fact - I've just had a look, and the registry keys your interested in 
are HKEY_CURRENT_USER/Console/ColorTable00 -> ColorTable15
These define the ARGB values for the console colours 0 through 15. I can't 
remember the exact order of the colours myself, but I know that 0 to 7 are 
the darker ones, and 8 to 15 are the exact same colours in a higher 
intensity form. It goes something like this:

0 Black    	8 Dark Grey
1 Red    	    	9 Light Red
2 Green    	10 Light Green
3 Cyan    	    	11 Light Cyan
4 Blue    	    	12 Light Blue
5 Magenta 	    	13 Light Magenta
6 Brown   	    	14 Yellow
7 Light Grey   	15 White

